/reserve/: ask for studio time on a week drawn from hosts.yml

The Studio half becomes a request form. It sends to the site-worker's existing `book` tank, so the
worker doesn't change.

- **Space:** Video Studio, Podcast Studio or Editing Bays, picked like a tab. Only the picked one's
  description shows. (The "Equipment Checkout" row is gone: the Equipment half is right beside it.)
- **Name and email:** check-in's profile on this phone (`fcpm.profile`). They fill the form, and
  sending writes them back, so the first request also sets up check-in.
- **Day, start, with:** a start time, always two hours. "With" lists everyone in `hosts.yml`, so
  anyone can be asked for.
- **The week:** one week at a time (This week / Next week / Week after), Tuesday to Saturday. Columns
  are `hosts.yml`'s `days` entries that have hours, in the file's order. Each person's day key is
  their hours. Hours are cut into two-hour slots with an hour between, so 11–4 is 11–1 and 2–4. Each
  slot shows the person's `supports`. The day runs from a quarter hour before the earliest slot to a
  quarter hour after the latest one ends. From today's file that is 10:45 to 7:15, because Thursday
  and Friday run 5–7. "Earlier" and "Later" strips above and below set 9 am or 7:30 pm, and focus
  the start box so it can be changed. A click in open space sets that time, to the quarter hour.
- **Host and time follow each other until both are picked by hand.** Picking a host with no time
  picks their next slot. Picking a slot with no host picks its host. A host picked by hand stays
  tilted, and the picked day's own host gets a yellow mark behind their card.
- **Changing week** stops drawing the pick but leaves it in the form.
- **The receipt** is kept on the phone (`fcpm.bookings`) and listed under the form ("Asked from this
  phone"). Nobody else's appointments are drawn.

`hosts.yml` is read as it is, through `jsonify`, and its format is unchanged. The worker's `book` tank
has no host field yet, so the host is written into `when`, e.g. "Saturday, November 7, 2026, 11 am to
1 pm, with Autumn".

Layout: on a wide screen the halves are now wider than the header, up to 94rem, and the studio gets
the larger share (1.25 : 1). On a phone the week scrolls sideways inside its half.

Fixes found along the way:
- `halves.js` took every `role="tab"` in the page, so the week tabs switched both halves off on a
  phone. It now reads only its own tab bar.
- On a phone, a wide child could widen the halves grid and the whole page. The grid column is now
  `minmax(0, 1fr)`.
- `answers.js` skips forms marked `data-sends`, which send themselves (book.js).

Merge qualifications:
- [x] `jekyll build` clean
- [x] secrets, internal-publish, tokens and no-code guards pass
- [x] Driven in headless Firefox, wide and phone: prefill from check-in, both follow rules, the hand-picked host
      kept with the day's host marked, week change, Earlier strip, open-space click, the send to `book`
      (stand-in worker), receipt, profile written back
- [ ] Playwright: 7 new tests in `reserve.spec.js` (time frozen to Monday 2 November). Their expected
      values were checked by hand with the same frozen time. Playwright can't run on digitization,
      so they get their first run here in CI.

Carried, not decided:
- No blocking yet: booked or unavailable slots still show as open.
- Whatever the worker keeps is emailed once the Microsoft 365 step is in place. Nothing here sends mail.
- Photos: a card shows `photo` if a person has one. None do yet.

